From: BLACK_MONDAY_WEB
Subject: [PATCH] ui_js: expose explicit EE frequency scale hook for mobile profiling

Pinned upstream: jpd002/Play-@83700b2c31e593bc94e845b4b31b797be84dda59

This does not change the default 1:1 PS2 timing. It only exposes Play!'s existing
CPS2VM::SetEeFrequencyScale API so the host can run opt-in compatibility/performance
experiments after Black Monday has a verified baseline.

--- a/Source/ui_js/Main.cpp
+++ b/Source/ui_js/Main.cpp
@@
 void clearStats()
 {
 	CStatsManager::GetInstance().ClearStats();
 }
+
+void setEeFrequencyScale(unsigned int numerator, unsigned int denominator)
+{
+	if(!g_virtualMachine) return;
+	if((numerator == 0) || (denominator == 0)) return;
+	g_virtualMachine->SetEeFrequencyScale(numerator, denominator);
+}
@@
 	function("clearStats", &clearStats);
+	function("setEeFrequencyScale", &setEeFrequencyScale);
 }
